## v0.25.9

### BOND_*/RECEIPT_CLAIM parity fixes verified behavior-neutral (2026-09-29)

Fleet-wide verification for the parallel-path parity fixes landed in
6026404775 (``feat(sync): … pure/sequential parity``): the ``transaction``
table holds zero ``BOND_*`` rows and zero ``RECEIPT_CLAIM`` rows ever
sealed on every host, so the BOND_* sequential-only correction and the
RECEIPT_CLAIM stale-ORM fix are behavior-neutral on all recorded history.
They change only what a *future* block containing such a transaction
would compute; no past block exercises either path, so no replay
divergence is possible.


### feat(market): derive the 1 AIT reference price instead of asserting it

- `aitbc/market/reference_price.py` (pure, no I/O) + `scripts/ops/ait-reference-price.py`: compute the 1 AIT = 1 compute-hour cost floor — reference-rig BOM amortized over a 3-year fully-booked lifetime + wall-draw electricity — and report the pinned price's margin over it (EUR 0.25 sits +44% over the EUR 0.173/h cost floor at EUR 1,530 BOM / 384 W / EUR 0.30 per kWh).
- `--write-json website/reference.json` emits the committed artifact; the exchange page renders it as the new "How the Reference Is Calculated" card and `exchange.js` now sources its REF_EUR from that file instead of a literal.
- The reference rig is documented as an island-level choice, not a protocol constant: cloners re-anchor via `--reset-components --component "Name=EUR"` plus a `GPU_COMPUTE_MULTIPLIER` rescale; `ait-value-model.md` carries the derived cost table and the re-derivation command.
- `tests/unit/test_reference_price.py`: 14 cases — defaults, utilization scaling, validation, JSON safety.


### Market sweepers: phantom-escrow fast fail (2026-10-04)

`746aa5a873`: an `ipfs_rental_token` whose job_id has no Escrow row
on-chain can never release or refund (observed live: an Aug-28 rental
recorded on the pre-Sep-3 chain). From the second deferred pass a
still-absent `verify_escrow` marks the row `settlement_failed` instead of
retrying to the 6h bound; present rows and probe failures keep the
bounded path. The three live phantom rows were terminal-marked by hand.


