## v0.25.3

### Unreleased — IPFS rental escrow lifecycle sweeper

- Decision: the marketplace service owns the IPFS rental escrow lifecycle, implemented as a dedicated `IpfsRentalSweeper` inside that service (not the coordinator's generic `StuckEscrowSweeper`).
- `IpfsRentalToken` model: added `pinned` (default `True`) and `tx_hash` fields; `status` supports `active`, `expired`, `released`, `refunded`, and `refund_pending`.
- `MarketplaceService.register_ipfs_rental_token`: canonicalizes `buyer_address` and `provider_address` to 0x EIP-55; defaults `pinned=True`.
- `apps/marketplace/src/marketplace_service/services/ipfs_rental_sweeper.py`: new sweeper that periodically scans for active rentals past `expires_at`, marks them `expired`, and releases escrow to the provider; refunds for `refund_pending` or `pinned=False`.
- `aitbc/marketplace/blockchain_rpc.py`: added `release_escrow` and `refund_escrow` RPC client methods.
- `apps/marketplace/src/marketplace_service/main.py`: lifespan now starts/stops the `IpfsRentalSweeper` background task.
- `apps/marketplace/tests/test_ipfs_rental_sweeper.py`: unit tests for release, refund, and skip-not-expired behavior.

## v0.24.18

### Fix — `aitbc-miner` default offer command uses `--service-type` options

The `aitbc market offer` command moved to option-style arguments
(`--service-type`, `--model-or-variant`, `--price`), but
`apps/miner/production_miner.py` still built the command with positional
arguments. This caused every default offer refresh on `<node2>` to fail with
`Missing option '--service-type'`.

Updated `publish_default_offers()` to pass the canonical option flags, keeping
`--unit` and `--description` as before. With `MINER_WALLET_ADDRESS` exported as
`SHOP_WALLET_ADDRESS`, the miner now successfully publishes (or skips when
identical) the Whisper, FFmpeg, and Ollama default offers.


## v0.24.16

### Phase 4 — Agent and discovery UX (2026-08-26)

- `aitbc agent status [AGENT_ID]` now defaults to the single local agent and
  lists local candidates when multiple agents exist.
- `aitbc agent inbox` now defaults to the single local agent when `--agent-id` is omitted.
- `aitbc agent discover agents` probes the coordinator first and prints a clear
  `sudo systemctl start aitbc-agent-coordinator` message when the service is down.
- `get_agent_status` now queries the coordinator and distinguishes a reachable
  coordinator that does not know the agent ("not registered") from an unreachable one.
- Live: pushed to Gitea and pulled on `<hub-node>` and `<node2>`;
  `aitbc agent status` without an agent_id resolves to the local default.


### Phase 6.2 — `aitbc ipfs host` paid pinning (2026-08-26)

- New `aitbc ipfs host <offer_id_or_plugin_id> <cid_or_file> --days N`.
  - Resolves an IPFS marketplace offer by `plugin_id` or `offer_id`.
  - Verifies `service_type == "ipfs"` and `price_unit == "per_day"`.
  - Uploads a file to the local Kubo API if a path is given, or uses the CID as-is.
  - Locks escrow for `price * days` using the wallet specified by `--wallet`.
  - Pins the CID on the local IPFS daemon and records the rental.
- `aitbc ipfs rentals` lists recorded rentals.
- `aitbc ipfs unpin <rental_id>` unpins a CID and can optionally request an
  escrow refund with `--refund`.

